📂 About the Dataset 
📘 Netflix Movies & TV Shows Dataset

This project uses the Netflix Titles Dataset from Kaggle, which contains information about Movies and TV Shows available on Netflix.

🔗 Dataset Source:
https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/shivamb/netflix-shows

📑 Dataset Description

| Column           | Description                                 |
| ---------------- | ------------------------------------------- |
| **show_id**      | Unique ID for every title                   |
| **type**         | Movie or TV Show                            |
| **title**        | Name of the content                         |
| **director**     | Director(s) of the title                    |
| **cast**         | Actors involved                             |
| **country**      | Country of production                       |
| **date_added**   | When the title was added to Netflix         |
| **release_year** | Year of original release                    |
| **rating**       | Age rating (TV-MA, PG, etc.)                |
| **duration**     | Movie length (minutes) or number of seasons |
| **listed_in**    | Genre(s)                                    |
| **description**  | Summary of the content                      |

📊 Why This Dataset Is Useful for Analysis

This dataset is widely used in data analytics because:

It includes both numeric and text data

It has missing values, which is good for practicing data cleaning

You can perform EDA (Exploratory Data Analysis) on:

genres

countries

movies vs TV shows

release years

content growth

It’s suitable for building visualizations

🧹 Common Data Cleaning Tasks in This Dataset

Filling missing values (director, cast, country)

Converting date_added to datetime

Splitting genres from the listed_in field

Extracting new features (year_added, main_genre)

Removing duplicates
